    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T04:07:54Z",
    "body": "The red changed. This run (44861277851) has one failed step: `motion suites: vertical_arc_entry`, both tests, at 0 s. It is a real deterministic failure, not the driver problem of the first comment: `concurrent_trace_callers_keep_the_gpu_lifecycle_safe` passed in this run.\n\nWhat changed: main moved 211105042 -> c310c4f61 with #3106 and with the batch of merge-ready PRs #2995, #3051, #3053, #3056, #3060, #3065, #3090. Each merged head was green alone (pr-test runs passed). The failure is therefore in the combination or in a merge order. The two test names read the entry-arc law (G18 arcs per level, chords on an oblique first cut), so start with the motion law commits in this batch, above all #3053 (lead_fit seam mirror) and #3065 (helical refusal gates) and #3090 (stock cap in the tilted frame).\n\n`git log --oneline 211105042..c310c4f61` lists the 9 merges. Bisect with `cargo xtask gate test vertical_arc_entry --crate motion`.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
